WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.422
SUBSTRING is useful when character position has a documented meaning.

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:10.347
For example, we may take the first three characters of a product name to build a teaching code.

00:00:10.347 --> 00:00:15.162
But fixed positions can be fragile when string structures vary.

00:00:15.162 --> 00:00:20.682
Use position-based extraction only when the structure is stable enough to justify it.

00:00:20.682 --> 00:00:25.267
String functions are most useful when the text has a predictable structure.

00:00:25.267 --> 00:00:30.597
Before extracting a substring, confirm the delimiter or pattern really exists.

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:36.312
Regular expressions are powerful, but a complicated regex can become hard to maintain;

00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:40.390
use the simplest rule that reliably matches the data you actually have.
